# Token map for the W4 report (DESIGN.md 6.4). Written from the fprintf formats of
# workloads/w4_heat_plate.m and the rules of reference_py/compare.py (RULES["w4_heat_plate"]),
# never from Sea output. Format: <line regex> <token number> <rule>. Tokens count from 1 on
# blank-separated fields; unlisted numeric tokens use the default rule (one unit of the last
# printed digit). The W4 JSON keys are in the report's units (K, degC, m, W, W/m^2), so
# `json <key>` applies directly.
#
# 'Grid %d x %d (h = %.3f mm), %d unknowns, %d coolant nodes, omega = %.5f'
# tokens: 2 nx, 4 ny, 7 h [mm] (default), 9 unknowns, 11 coolant nodes, 16 omega (no RULES
# entry: compare.py's DEFAULT, 1e-9 relative, is below one printed unit, so the default rule).
^Grid[[:space:]]   2    json nx
^Grid[[:space:]]   4    json ny
^Grid[[:space:]]   9    json n_unknown
^Grid[[:space:]]   11   json n_hole
#
# 'Scalar SOR    : %5d sweeps, last change %.3e K, max residual %.3e K' (and 'Red-black SOR :').
# Token 3 is the lone ':'; token 4 the sweep count (it_sor / it_rb int 1); token 8 the last
# change, which has no JSON key: both runs stop with it at or below tol = 1e-8 K, so the rule is
# that bound, num 1e-8 0 (as the `small` rules of the residuals; an iteration count changed by
# one moves it within that bound); token 12 the max residual (res_sor / res_rb small 1e-7).
^Scalar[[:space:]]SOR[[:space:]]   4    json it_sor
^Scalar[[:space:]]SOR[[:space:]]   8    num 1e-8 0
^Scalar[[:space:]]SOR[[:space:]]   12   json res_sor
^Red-black[[:space:]]SOR[[:space:]]   4    json it_rb
^Red-black[[:space:]]SOR[[:space:]]   8    num 1e-8 0
^Red-black[[:space:]]SOR[[:space:]]   12   json res_rb
#
# 'Max difference between the two solutions: %.3e K': token 7, diff_solvers small 1e-5.
^Max[[:space:]]difference   7    json diff_solvers
#
# 'Hot spot %.4f degC at (x, y) = (%.4f, %.4f) m': token 3 T_max (num 1e-6 absolute), tokens 9
# '(0.0825,' and 10 '0.0938)' the position (x_Tmax / y_Tmax exact: the same grid node).
^Hot[[:space:]]spot   3    json T_max
^Hot[[:space:]]spot   9    json x_Tmax
^Hot[[:space:]]spot   10   json y_Tmax
#
# 'T mean %.4f degC over the unknown nodes': token 3, T_mean num 1e-6 absolute.
^T[[:space:]]mean   3    json T_mean
#
# The heat-flow table '  %-16s %12.6f': every label but 'balance' is two words, so the value is
# token 3 (token 2 for 'balance'). Q_bottom / Q_top / Q_hole num 1e-4 absolute, Q_gen 1e-12
# relative, Q_balance small 1e-5.
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]bottom[[:space:]]edge       3    json Q_bottom
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]top[[:space:]]edge          3    json Q_top
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]coolant[[:space:]]channel   3    json Q_hole
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]heat[[:space:]]source       3    json Q_gen
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]balance                     2    json Q_balance
#
# 'Peak heat flux %.4e W/m^2 at (x, y) = (%.4f, %.4f) m': token 4 q_max (1e-7 relative), tokens
# 10 and 11 the position (x_qmax / y_qmax exact). Token 5 'W/m^2' is non-numeric and identical.
^Peak[[:space:]]heat[[:space:]]flux   4    json q_max
^Peak[[:space:]]heat[[:space:]]flux   10   json x_qmax
^Peak[[:space:]]heat[[:space:]]flux   11   json y_qmax
